<section class="hero" id="home"><div class="wrap"><div class="hero-content">
<div class="eyebrow">A generation with purpose</div>
<h1>Empowering the Future.</h1>
<p>Building a united, informed and empowered generation of young people working together for the development of Madi Opei.</p>
<div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn light" href="#about">Discover MOYA <span>→</span></a><a class="btn outline" href="#join">Join our association</a></div>
<div class="hero-note"><span>✦</span><span><strong>One community. One vision.</strong> A stronger future starts with us.</span></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="section" id="about"><div class="wrap about-grid">
<div class="photo-stack"><div class="photo-main"></div><div class="photo-small"></div><div class="quote">UNITY • SERVICE • PROGRESS</div></div>
<div><div class="section-head"><div class="kicker">Who we are</div><h2>Young people united for community progress.</h2><p>Madi Opei Youth Association (MOYA) is a registered Community Based Organisation (CBO) in Madi Opei Town Council, Lamwo District, Uganda. We bring young people together to participate in positive community action, leadership, development and mutual support.</p></div>
<p class="muted">Our work is guided by the belief that young people are not only leaders of tomorrow, but active contributors to the community today.</p>
<div class="values"><div class="value"><b>Our vision</b><span>An empowered and united youth community.</span></div><div class="value"><b>Our mission</b><span>Mobilising youth for meaningful development.</span></div><div class="value"><b>Our motto</b><span>Empowering the Future.</span></div></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="section soft" id="programmes"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div class="kicker">What we do</div><h2>Turning youth energy into positive action.</h2><p>MOYA creates opportunities for young people to learn, participate, lead and contribute to the wellbeing of Madi Opei.</p></div>
<div class="cards">
<div class="card"><div class="icon">🌱</div><h3>Youth empowerment</h3><p>Encouraging skills development, responsible leadership, initiative and participation in community development.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="icon">🤝</div><h3>Community support</h3><p>Promoting solidarity, volunteerism and collective action when members and families in our community need support.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="icon">⚽</div><h3>Sports &amp; recreation</h3><p>Using sports to build teamwork, discipline, talent, friendship and positive relationships among young people.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="icon">🌾</div><h3>Agriculture &amp; food security</h3><p>Promoting household and community food security through agricultural activities, including cassava growing, sesame (simsim) production and planned coffee production. We encourage productive farming, learning and collective participation.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="icon">📚</div><h3>Learning &amp; awareness</h3><p>Creating spaces for dialogue, mentorship, awareness and exchange of ideas on issues affecting young people.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="icon">🎉</div><h3>Annual youth gathering</h3><p>Bringing the community together to celebrate youth, share ideas, recognise achievements and plan for the future.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="icon">🌍</div><h3>Partnerships</h3><p>Connecting with institutions, organisations, development partners and well-wishers who share our community vision.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="section soft" id="leadership"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Governance</div><h2>Executive Leadership</h2><p class="lead">Meet the MOYA executive team, committed to accountable leadership and service to young people and the wider community.</p><div class="grid">
<div class="card person"><img src="chairperson-philips.png" alt="Rubangakene Philips, Chairperson"><div class="info"><h3>Rubangakene Philips</h3><div class="role">Chairperson</div><p class="small">Contact: +256 789 813 592</p></div></div>
<div class="card person"><img src="olak-mercy.jpg" alt="Olak Mercy, Vice Chairperson"><div class="info"><h3>Olak Mercy</h3><div class="role">Vice Chairperson</div></div></div>
<div class="card person"><img src="atimango-sicola.jpg" alt="Atimango Sicola, Secretary"><div class="info"><h3>Atimango Sicola</h3><div class="role">Secretary</div></div></div>
<div class="card person"><img src="ajalo-gloria.jpg" alt="Ajalo Gloria, Vice Secretary"><div class="info"><h3>Ajalo Gloria</h3><div class="role">Vice Secretary</div></div></div>
<div class="card person"><img src="ojara-henry.jpg" alt="Ojara Henry, Treasurer"><div class="info"><h3>Ojara Henry</h3><div class="role">Treasurer</div><p class="small">Contact: 0783502982</p></div></div>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="mentor"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Guidance and experience</div><h2>Mentorship and Advisory</h2><p class="lead">MOYA recognises mentorship as an important part of youth growth and responsible leadership.</p><div class="grid"><div class="card person"><img src="mentor-jamesson.jpg" alt="Jamesson Dennish Onekalit, MOYA Mentor"><div class="info"><h3>Jamesson Dennish Onekalit</h3><div class="role">Mentor / Adviser</div><p class="small">Contact: +256 774 240 242</p></div></div><div class="card"><h3>Guiding the next generation</h3><p>Through guidance, lived experience and encouragement, our mentor supports young people to pursue self-discovery, responsible leadership, gratitude, personal growth and service to the community.</p><p class="small">Mentorship is distinct from the elected executive offices and strengthens the association through advice and intergenerational guidance.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section soft" id="events"><div class="wrap"><div class="notice"><div><div class="eyebrow">Save the date • 2026</div><h2>Madi Opei Youth Annual Gathering</h2><p>The second edition is scheduled for 27 December 2026. A time for connection, community conversation, youth recognition and renewed commitment to our shared future. Further programme details will be announced by the organising team.</p></div><div class="event-date"><b>27</b><span>December 2026</span></div></div>
<div style="margin-top:25px" class="cards">
<div class="card"><div class="icon">🏆</div><h3>Madi Opei Premier League</h3><p>Celebrating local football, teamwork and healthy competition through a partnership between Madi Opei Youth Association (MOYA), Madi Opei Development Association (MODA) and the Office of Ker Kal Kwaro Madi Opei.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="icon">🫶</div><h3>Community wellbeing</h3><p>Encouraging care, unity and practical support for members of our community.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="icon">🎤</div><h3>Youth dialogue</h3><p>Making room for conversations about leadership, opportunity and the future of Madi Opei.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

